{
  "id": "V08",
  "title": "Two-story aligned stack",
  "intent": "Two solid walls stacked with both ends aligned. The top wall end forces go into the bottom wall ends per combination and add to its own; the base hardware and posts are sized for the sum. Also: strap (MSTC) at the upper floor line, holdown (HDUE) at the foundation, and a combination with live load that does not govern.",
  "covers": [
    "Story shear build-up",
    "Wall end transfer at aligned ends (±0.1 ft)",
    "Per-combination accumulation",
    "MSTC strap (16\" floor span)",
    "HDUE + minimum post",
    "ASCE 7-22 §2.4.5 (5), (6), (8)"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Story shears: Roof V_T = 3 k; Level 1 V_B = 3 + 4 = 7 k. One wall per story takes all of it."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "SW-1 (Roof, L = 10 ft, h = 9 ft): v = 0.7 × 3000 / 10 = 210.00 plf → 6\" o.c. (312 plf). SW-2 (Level 1, h = 10 ft): v = 0.7 × 7000 / 10 = 490.00 plf → 4\" o.c. 470 < 489.9999999999999 NG → 3\" o.c. (611 plf)."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "SW-1 gravity: D = 100 plf × 10 + 10 psf × 10 × 9 = 1.90 k → R_D = 0.95 k per end; Lr = 50 × 10 = 0.50 k → 0.25 k per end. M_OT = 3 × 9 = 27 k·ft → N_E = ±2.70 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "SW-1 uplift (0.6 − 0.14S_DS)D + 0.7E: 0.46 × 0.95 − 0.7 × 2.70 = -1.453 → T = 1.453 k at the Roof floor line (not the bottom story → strap) → lightest MSTC (16\" span) ≥ 1453 lb: MSTC28 (1535 lb)."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "SW-1 compression: combo (5) 1.14 × 0.95 + 0.7 × 2.70 = 2.973 k; combo (6) 1.105 × 0.95 + 0.525 × 2.70 = 2.467 k; D + Lr = 1.200 k → C = 2.973 k → post (MSTC minimum (2)2x4) (2)2x4 at 9 ft (cap 6.03 k)."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "SW-2 own gravity: D = 80 × 10 + 10 × 10 × 10 = 1.80 k → 0.90 k per end; L = 150 × 10 = 1.50 k → 0.75 k per end. M_OT = 7 × 10 = 70 k·ft → N_E = ±7.00 k. Load case 1.0D at each SW-2 end incl. SW-1 above = 0.90 + 0.95 = 1.85 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Base uplift = own + SW-1 end, same combination. (8): [0.46 × 0.90 − 0.7 × 7.00] + [-1.453] = -5.939; (6): [1.105 × 0.90 + 0.75 × 0.75 − 0.525 × 7.00] + [1.105 × 0.95 − 0.525 × 2.70] = -2.486 → T = 5.939 k → HDUE7 (7015 lb; HDUE5 5375 lb too small)."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Base compression: (5) 1.14 × 0.90 + 0.7 × 7.00 + 2.973 = 8.899 k; (6) 1.105 × 0.90 + 0.75 × 0.75 + 0.525 × 7.00 + 2.467 = 7.699 k; D + L = 2.600 k → C = 8.899 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "Base post (HDUE7 minimum (2)2x4, 10 ft): lightest with cap ≥ 8.90 k in the order (2)2x4, (3)2x4, 4x4, 6x4, 8x4 → 6x4 (cap 9.14 k)."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "Line checks: base shear 7 k, base moment Σ V·h = 3 × 9 + 7 × 10 = 97 k·ft; all gravity reaches the foundation → G1–G12 pass."
    },
    {
      "step": 11,
      "text": "SW-1 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 3.000 / 10 = 300.00 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 16 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0098; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.1688; Δ_HD = 0.0808 × 2700.00 / 1535/0.7 = 0.0995 (MSTC28, T = 2700.00 lb); r = 2700.00 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.4114 → Δ_c = 0.0113; h·Δa/b = 9 × (0.0995 + 0.0113) / 10 = 0.0997 → δ = 0.2782 in. (strap slip at its LRFD cap = cap / 0.7.)"
    },
    {
      "step": 12,
      "text": "SW-2 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 7.000 / 10 = 700.00 plf, A = 19.25 in², G_a = 22 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0171; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.3182; Δ_HD = 0.154 × 9700.00 / 7015 (ASD cap) = 0.2129 (HDUE7, T = 9700.00 lb); r = 9700.00 / (19.25 × 625) = 0.8062 → Δ_c = 0.0256; h·Δa/b = 10 × (0.2129 + 0.0256) / 10 = 0.2386 → δ = 0.5739 in. (T = C = N_B + N_T = 7.000 + 2.700 = 9.700 k: the SW-1 end force adds to SW-2's own.)"
    },
    {
      "step": 13,
      "text": "Story drift Roof: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-1 0.2782 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.2782 / 1.0 = 1.113 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 9 × 12 = 2.160 in → OK."
    },
    {
      "step": 14,
      "text": "Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-2 0.5739 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.5739 / 1.0 = 2.296 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → OK."
    }
  ],
